/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.profraw

github-token.txt
/tmp

# Fuzzing: the corpus and crash artefacts are large and machine-generated. Crashers
# that matter are promoted into `tests/regression/` as committed fixtures instead,
# so a reproducer never lives only in an ignored directory.
/fuzz/target
/fuzz/Cargo.lock
/fuzz/artifacts
/fuzz/corpus

# Comparison-harness output: renders, diffs and heatmaps are regenerated on demand.
/target/pdfref

# Two things, one rule: nothing fetched from somebody else's server is tracked here.
# `corpus-cache/safedocs/` is what `tools/safedocs` writes — members of the SafeDocs
# `CC-MAIN-2021-31` archives, taken a byte range at a time, with `manifest.tsv` beside them
# recording the archive, the member name and the SHA-256 so that any of them can be fetched
# again exactly. Those files are somebody's web pages under no licence anybody granted, which
# is the reason this line is a licence position rather than a size one: a file promoted out of
# here into the tree is a deliberate act with its own argument (ADR 0258,
# doc/third-party-data.md). The four test corpora that *are* tracked are submodules under
# doc/corpora/, which carry no bytes into this history at all.
/corpus-cache

# The specifications this project is written against, and the Markdown conversion of them
# that the citation checker reads. Free to obtain from the PDF Association, not free to
# redistribute — so the repository carries them only inside doc/specifications.zip, which is
# encrypted and is tracked (ADR 0187, NOTICE section 3). What `unzip` puts here is ignored.
#
# `/doc/md` carries no trailing slash deliberately: a worktree round symlinks it to the main
# checkout's copy rather than unzipping a second one, and a pattern ending in `/` matches a
# directory but not a symlink to one — so the specifications showed up as untracked, which is
# exactly the state this rule exists to prevent.
/doc/*.pdf
/doc/md

# What `tools/spec-errata` emits from those PDFs: the annotations the conversion dropped, which
# are the errata themselves. Derived from the same documents under the same licence, so it goes
# under the same rule — and it is regenerated in six seconds, so nothing is lost by not carrying
# it (ADR 0252).
/doc/errata.md

# Claude Code local settings (per-user, not shared).
.claude/settings.local.json

# A local checkout of another renderer, kept beside the tree for comparison and not
# vendored into it: 93 218 lines of third-party source with C, CUDA and Vulkan
# dependencies this project does not take. What was measured from it is in ADR 0136,
# which is the part that has to survive the directory being deleted.
/doc/rasterrocket

# A worktree round names its build directory here rather than exporting CARGO_TARGET_DIR
# (ADR 0344: an exported CARGO_* empties the sccache cache). The file is the round's own.
.cargo/config.toml
